{"status":"completed","summary":"Published the staged public and staff trees on node1 TCP port 8080. Public content is anonymous; staff content requires HTTP Basic authentication as reader. The service survives node restart, runs unprivileged, and preserves the legacy OS, kernel, and supplied files.","actions_performed":["Installed a Python 2.5-compatible HTTP service using the existing runtime.","Configured SysV startup for runlevels 2–5.","Protected /staff/ and all staff files with HTTP Basic authentication.","Disabled directory listings and restricted serving to the public and staff trees.","Rebooted node1 and verified automatic recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Public content is anonymously available on TCP port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-83a94587fb964713","cmd-452ac93eedb646ed"],"summary":"Before and after reboot, the service listened on 0.0.0.0:8080 and /public/ returned HTTP 200 with an exact match to the staged index."},{"requirement":"Staff content requires reader Basic authentication","command_ids":["cmd-83a94587fb964713","cmd-452ac93eedb646ed"],"summary":"Anonymous and incorrect-password requests returned 401 without exposing staff content; valid reader credentials returned exact copies of the staged staff index and roster."},{"requirement":"Password file and directory listings are not served","command_ids":["cmd-83a94587fb964713","cmd-452ac93eedb646ed"],"summary":"Direct and encoded-traversal requests for access.txt returned 404; /public/ served its index with no directory-listing markers."},{"requirement":"Supplied pages remain intact and the legacy platform is retained","command_ids":["cmd-82a1e9e3ce904bd3","cmd-83a94587fb964713","cmd-452ac93eedb646ed"],"summary":"The four supplied files retained their paths, sizes, ownership, and permissions; served pages matched their staged sources. Kernel remained 2.6.22-14-generic."},{"requirement":"Service starts automatically and runs with reduced privilege","command_ids":["cmd-0e599359205f451b","cmd-452ac93eedb646ed"],"summary":"SysV startup links were installed; after reboot the service returned automatically and ran as nobody."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-83a94587fb964713","cmd-58eafe5eb2d74252","cmd-563573e2034d4a01","cmd-452ac93eedb646ed"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 7954dab4-7c96-41fa-a1b7-63a2f6aa4e29 was captured, reboot was acknowledged, boot ID changed to a5c705b9-ea61-4531-93a7-3d072f3768ea, and full service, authentication, content, and data recovery were verified."}]}
